          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Primary, inherited (or familial), bilateral, and often symmetric condition of the cornea that is not associated with other ocular or",
              "pdf_page": 419,
              "printed_page": 337,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "systemic diseases.",
              "pdf_page": 419,
              "printed_page": 337,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Three types based on anatomic location—epithelial: characterized by dyskeratotic and necrotic epithelial cells, focal absence of epithelial basement membrane, and cell infiltrate in anterior corneal stroma; stromal: lipid deposition within corneal stroma; endothelial: characterized by abnormal, dystrophic endothelial cells.",
              "pdf_page": 419,
              "printed_page": 337,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
